  "id": "Compound::DB00238 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Nevirapine and Cyp2c9, mediated through the compound Delavirdine, which is included in the class of Non-nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors. This pathway is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Nevirapine and its analogs, such as Delavirdine, bind to Cyp2c9. The lowest common ancestor of these entities is the Organic Heteropolycyclic Compound, reinforcing the shared structural and functional characteristics of these compounds. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent level of confidence in the association, though the exact mechanism of binding remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence highlights the role of these compounds in modulating Cyp2c9 activity, which is relevant to drug metabolism and pharmacokinetics. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader class of Non-nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors in understanding their interaction with Cyp2c9.",
